{"authored" [{"question" "q-66902" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that ${e}^{-5z}-6=-2,$ find the value of $z$ rounded to $3$ decimal places." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930137/state.json" "file_sha256" "809a34a3f48f76ed1bd98c492f98a7c80ed3f9a13acc12e223cd017c4f0fde6c" "basis" 318 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930137/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-66902" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rearrange our equation into a form that is more convenient for logarithms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-5z}-6 & =-2 \\\\ {e}^{-5z} & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we find the natural logarithm $(ln)$ of both sides of the equation and solve for $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-5z} & =4 \\\\ ln⁡({e}^{-5z}) & =ln⁡(4) \\\\ -5z & =ln⁡(4) \\\\ z & =-\\frac{1}{5}ln⁡(4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $z=-\\frac{1}{5}ln⁡(4)$\n\nEvaluating the above expression using a calculator gives\n\n$$\nz≈-0.277\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930137/state.json" "file_sha256" "809a34a3f48f76ed1bd98c492f98a7c80ed3f9a13acc12e223cd017c4f0fde6c" "basis" 318 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930137/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-66902" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930137/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "928dda5a1cc7074ac6158d502b6d0660fc7156e5da3d028a7faa049a722f3f01" "basis" 318 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930137/edb-import/verification.json"} {"q