:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3x} & =9 \\\\ ln⁡({e}^{3x}) & =ln⁡(9) \\\\ 3x & =ln⁡(9) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{3}ln⁡(9)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the above expression using a calculator gives\n\n$$\nx≈0.732\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930137/state.json" "file_sha256" "809a34a3f48f76ed1bd98c492f98a7c80ed3f9a13acc12e223cd017c4f0fde6c" "basis" 318 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930137/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-263077" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930137/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "928dda5a1cc7074ac6158d502b6d0660fc7156e5da3d028a7faa049a722f3f01" "basis" 318 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930137/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-263077" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930137/state.json" "file_sha256" "809a34a3f48f76ed1bd98c492f98a7c80ed3f9a13acc12e223cd017c4f0fde6c" "basis" 318 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930137/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-263081" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If ${e}^{5-y/2}=\\sqrt[5]{7},$ then $y≈${{field-1}}, rounded to $3$ decimal places." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930137/state.json" "file_sha256" "809a34a3f48f76ed1bd98c492f98a7c80ed3f9a13acc12e223cd017c4f0fde6c" "basis" 318 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930137/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-263081" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we take $ln$ of both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{5-y/2} & =\\sqrt[5]{7} \\\\ ln⁡({e}^{5-y/2}) & =ln⁡(\\sqrt[5]{7}) \\\\ 5-\\frac{y}{2} & =ln⁡({7}^{1/5})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the power rule to the right-hand side and solve for $y:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5-\\frac{y}{2} & =\\frac{1}{5}ln⁡(7) \\\\ -\\frac{y}{2} & =\\frac{1}{5}ln⁡(7)-5 \\\\ y & =-\\frac{2}{5}ln⁡(7)+10\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the above expression using a calculator gives\n\n$$\ny≈9.222\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930137/state.json" "file_sha256" "809a34a3f48f76ed1bd98c492f98a7c80ed3f9a13acc12e223cd017c4f0fde6c" "basis" 318 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930137/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-263081" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930137/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "928dda5a1cc7074ac6158d502b6d0660fc7156e5da3d028a7faa049a722f3f01" "basis" 318 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930137/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-263081" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930137/state.json" "file_sha256" "809a34a3f48f76ed1bd98c492f98a7c80ed3f9a13acc12e223cd017c4f0fde6c" "basis" 318 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930137/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-263081" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "9.222"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930137/state.json" "file_sha256" "809a34a3f48f76ed1bd98c492f98a7c80ed3f9a13acc12e223cd017c4f0fde6c" "basis" 318 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930137/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-263199" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If $9-{e}^{3-4x}=5,$ then $x≈${{field-1}}, rounded to $3$ decimal places." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930137/state.json" "file_sha256" "809a34a3f48f76ed1bd98c492f98a7c80ed3f9a13acc12e223cd017c4f0fde6c" "basis" 318 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930137/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-263199" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rearrange our equation into a form that is more convenient for logarithms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9-{e}^{3-4x} & =5 \\\\ -{e}^{3-4x} & =5-9 \\\\ -{e}^{3-4x} & =-4 \\\\ {e}^{3-4x} & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we find the natural logarithm $(ln)$ of both sides of the equation and solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{3-4x} & =4 \\\\ ln⁡({e}^{3-4x}) & =ln⁡(4) \\\\ 3-4x & =ln⁡(4) \\\\ -4x & =ln⁡(4)-3 \\\\ x & =-\\frac{1}{4}ln⁡(4)+\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the above expression using a calculator gives\n\n$$\nx≈0.403\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930137/state.json" "file_sha256" "809a34a3f48f76ed1bd98c492f98a7c80ed3f9a13acc12e223cd017c4f0fde6c" "basis" 318 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930137/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-263199" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930137/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "928dda5a1cc7074ac6158d502b6d0660fc7156e5da3d028a7faa049a722f3f01" "basis" 318 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930137/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-263199" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930137/state.json" "file_sha256" "809a34a3f48f76ed1bd98c492f98a7c80ed3f9a13acc12e223cd017c4f0fde6c" "basis" 318 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930137/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-263199" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0.403"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930137/state.json" "file_sha256" "809a34a3f48f76ed1bd98c492f98a7c80ed3f9a13acc12e223cd017c4f0fde6c" "basis" 318 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930137/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-66902" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that ${e}^{-5z}-6=-2,$ find the value of $z$ rounded to $3$ decimal places." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930137/state.json" "file_sha256" "809a34a3f48f76ed1bd98c492f98a7c80ed3f9a13acc12e223cd017c4f0fde6c"} {"question" "q-66902" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we rearrange our equation into a form that is more convenient for logarithms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-5z}-6 & =-2 \\\\ {e}^{-5z} & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we find the natural logarithm $(ln)$ of both sides of the equation and solve for $z:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-5z} & =4 \\\\ ln⁡({e}^{-5z}) & =ln⁡(4) \\\\ -5z & =ln⁡(4) \\\\ z & =-\\frac{1}{5}ln⁡(4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $z=-\\frac{1}{5}ln⁡(4)$\n\nEvaluating the above expression using a calculator gives\n\n$$\nz≈-0.277\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930137/state.json" "file_sha256" "809a34a3f48f76ed1bd98c492f98a7c80ed3f9a13acc12e223cd017c4f0fde6c"} {"question" "q-66902" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930137/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "928dda5a1cc7074ac6158d502b6d0660fc7156e5da3d028a7faa049a722f3f01"} {"question" "q-66902" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930137/state.json" "file_sha256" "809a34a3f48f76ed1bd98c492f98a7c80ed3f9a13acc12e223cd017c4f0fde6c"} {"question" "q-66902" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-0.277"] ["math" "-0.554"] ["math" "0.277"] ["math" "0.554"] ["math" "0.727"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930137/state.json" "file_sha256" "809a34a3f48f76ed1bd98c492f98a7c80ed3f9a13acc12e223cd017c4f0fde6c"} {"question" "q-66902" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-0.277"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13930137/state.json" "file_sha256" "809a34a3f48f76ed1bd98c492f98a7c80ed3f9a13acc12e223cd017c4f0fde6c"} {"question" "q-228897" "field" n